# RAG / vector store

Authoritative spec: `spec/architecture.md`, `spec/rag-ingestion.md`, `spec/rag-api-contract.md`, `spec/evaluation-strategy.md`.

## Stores

- **MySQL** is the system of record for tickets, comments, resolution, and `TicketIndexingState`.
- **PostgreSQL + PGVector** holds derived chunks/embeddings only. Never read ticket truth from PGVector.
- Do not store embeddings as MySQL JSON/BLOB. Do not migrate Bootcamp to PostgreSQL.

## Knowledge

- Index only support-ticket text: title, description, ordered comments, resolution when present, plus labeled status/priority/assignee/category.
- Never index Bootcamp resources, FAQs, web content, or other app entities.

Canonical sections, stable order: Ticket ID, Title, Description, Status, Priority, Assignee (`UNASSIGNED` or user display), Category, Comments, Resolution (if present).

Chunk metadata (all required): `ticketId`, `ticketVersion` (= ticket JPA `@Version`), `chunkIndex`, `status`, `priority`, `assigneeId` (nullable), `assigneeDisplay` (never null), `category`.

- One ticket per chunk. Configurable chunk size/overlap. Vector dimension matches the chosen embedding model.

## Retrieval and generation (single flow, not an agent)

1. Embed the question.
2. PGVector similarity search, limit **configured top-K**, drop scores below **configured threshold**.
3. If none remain: return no-relevant-tickets (`relevantTicketsFound: false`, empty `sources`) and **do not call** the chat model.
4. Else one generation using **only** qualifying chunks. No tools, no web, no general knowledge as ticket fact.
5. `sources[].ticketId` must be a subset of retrieved qualifying IDs. Strip any other IDs.

Do not add generic metadata pre-filters. Metadata is for grounding, citations, eval, and future use.

Endpoint: `POST /api/ai/ask` with `{ "question": "..." }`.

## Freshness

On create, title/description/priority/assignee/category/comment/resolution/status/soft-delete: same MySQL tx writes data + `PENDING` (`requestedVersion` = ticket `@Version`). Embed/replace **after commit**. Replace all chunks for that ticket in one PGVector tx. Do not overwrite a newer indexed `@Version`. Simple in-process retry only — no Kafka, RabbitMQ, Quartz, or admin retry API.

## Providers

Keep provider/model abstract (Ollama vs cloud). Config only; never commit API keys. Changing embedding dimension requires re-index. Evaluate grounding with `spec/evaluation-strategy.md`; do not treat “looks right” as pass.
